cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "sativa-epang: SATIVA with EPA-ng as the placement engine"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both this record and the original
  SATIVA paper (Kozlov et al. 2016), whose algorithm it implements.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Auguste
    family-names: Gardette
    email: auguste.gardette@ird.fr
    affiliation: "UMMISCO, IRD / Sorbonne Université, France"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Aaramis/sativa-epang"
url: "https://github.com/Aaramis/sativa-epang/blob/epa-ng/CHANGES-epa-ng.md"
version: 0.9.3.4
date-released: "2026-08-27"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - taxonomy
  - phylogenetic placement
  - reference database curation
  - mislabel detection
  - 16S rRNA
  - ITS
abstract: >-
  A fork of SATIVA (Kozlov et al. 2016) that replaces the RAxML placement
  engine with EPA-ng (Barbera et al. 2019) in both the leave-one-out and the
  final confirmation pass, while leaving SATIVA's classification and decision
  logic unchanged: EPA-ng edges are mapped back onto SATIVA's own branch
  numbering by leaf bipartition. Measured against unmodified SATIVA v0.9.3 on
  ITS alignments, the leave-one-out drops from 257 s to 15.4 s at 1600
  sequences and from 1536 s to 87 s at 5402, with 0.98 recall and 0.90
  precision at 800 sequences. The leave-one-out can also be driven one step at
  a time, so a workflow manager can build the reference, prepare the folds,
  place them across a cluster and score the result as separate jobs, with
  byte-identical output either way. Distributed through Bioconda as
  sativa-epang.
